cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pldsc, please cite the software plus the method references below; the full method landscape (Popcorn, S-LDXR, MAMA, cov-LDSC and the 2026 meta-LDSC preprint) is maintained in docs/STRATEGY.md §5 and docs/PRIOR_ART.md."
title: "PLDSC: fast LD Score regression and population structure research"
abstract: >-
  PLDSC provides univariate and bivariate LD Score regression with optional
  Numba acceleration and allelign-backed GWAS QC and harmonization. It also
  studies LD scores for multi-ancestry meta-analyses and the effect of
  reference mismatch. Panel-based kappa is a plug-in slope comparison,
  not a calibrated estimate of absolute heritability bias. The package
  retains the tested mixed-model and LD-score tools and the historical
  negative-results record from its archived estimator research line.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vilhjálmsson"
    given-names: "Bjarni Jóhann"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bvilhjal/PLDSC"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0.dev3
